# Files that are read by Linux tooling keep LF even when checked out on
# Windows. A Dockerfile with CRLF line endings is the classic case: the RUN
# steps here use backslash continuations, and a carriage return after one has
# historically broken parsers. Modern BuildKit copes, but there is no reason to
# rely on that when building from a Windows working tree under WSL.
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf

# Everything else follows the platform default.
* text=auto
